  <figcaption class="kh-figure__caption">Castle: the first pass against the concept, the third pass, and the concept itself. The right motifs at sticker size.</figcaption>
</figure>

4. **Paint over.** A new `npm run paint-over` tool shrinks a crop of the concept back to 1× pixels: each output pixel takes the most common palette colour in its block, so one-pixel outlines survive. Then the result is cleaned up by hand: one crisp outline, JPEG speckles voted out, stone redrawn on a grid so it tiles.

The concepts came out at 2.5 to 3.7 screen pixels per art pixel, so the first step of a paint-over is measuring that.

<figure class="kh-figure">
