## Bonn

Bonn got the most attention, because it is where I live. The first version had the right buildings, but you had to be told which was which. It now has the Minster with its octagonal tower and spire, the pink Altes Rathaus with its double staircase, the Post Tower in two offset glass halves, and Langer Eugen beside it, where I took [this sunrise](/posts/20261005-sunrise-over-siebengebirge/). Beethoven stands on a plinth by the cherry blossom, after the monument on Münsterplatz. The zoom box is a shield inspired by the city's arms: a black cross on white over a gold lion on red. It is an emblem, not the arms, and the scheme is not official.

